    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling outfield contingent, headlined by **Taylor Ward** (70.17) and **Lawrence Butler** (69.27). **Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Rea, while **Butler** maintains strong efficiency through a high-value platoon advantage (+13%). **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) also stands out; his raw power against Rea is bolstered by a significant +7% platoon edge, making him a critical piece in our pursuit of 5x5 production despite the inherent risk of facing an elite hold pitcher. **Cal Raleigh** remains our top internal anchor at catcher, leveraging a +19% SP skill advantage against Phillips to comfortably clear the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's roster card involved keeping **Jung Hoo Lee** (42.41) on the bench. While he carries the inherent speed profile we covet, his matchup against Cease\u2014one of the tougher arms on the docket\u2014suppressed his efficiency relative to the higher-floor production of **Zack Gelof** (58.18) and **Jonathan Aranda** (58.16). We are monitoring the risk factors for **Masyn Winn** (41.31) and **Luis Arraez** (41.06), both of whom are operating near the bottom of our start-worthy range due to the SP skill of Harrison and Cease, respectively. **Bryce Harper** (56.59) remains a locked-in utility play; despite the difficult matchup against Burns, his elite 0.404 xwOBA baseline provides a necessary cushion against a potentially volatile outcome. No major weather alerts are impacting our lineup, though we remain hyper-aware that our SB-heavy strategy relies heavily on these fringe starters maintaining their aggressive base-running presence early in the count.",
